# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public bundle vars — Vite injects these into the browser JS at build time.
# Treat as PUBLIC: anyone visiting the deployed site can read them with
# DevTools. Restrict them via referer / origin policy on the provider side.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: applet URL. AI Studio injects it at runtime; leave blank for
# local dev to fall back to window.location.origin.
APP_URL=""

# NOTE: VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY is INTENTIONALLY NOT here. As of the proxy
# refactor, all Gemini calls go through the server-side Pages Function at
# /api/ai/relay. The browser never sees the key. Set `GEMINI_API_KEY`
# below as a Cloudflare env binding instead.
#
# Same applies to the Smithsonian key — it's now a server-side binding,
# not VITE_-prefixed. The Library scraper calls /api/scraper/smithsonian/*.

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend secrets — NEVER prefix with VITE_. Set via the Cloudflare Pages
# dashboard ("Settings → Environment variables → Secrets") OR locally with:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
# For local dev with `npm run dev:full`, drop them in `.dev.vars` (gitignored).
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Server-side Gemini API key. Read by functions/api/ai/relay.ts ONLY.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# Smithsonian Open Access — api.data.gov key for the Library panel scraper.
# Read only by functions/api/scraper/smithsonian/*.
# Get one at https://api.data.gov/signup/
SMITHSONIAN_API_KEY=""

# Google OAuth 2.0 client credentials (used by /api/auth/login + /api/auth/callback).
# The OAuth flow uses PKCE (RFC 7636) — no extra client setup needed.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# JWT signing secret. Must be ≥ 32 bytes of entropy.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=""

# Optional: Modal-hosted CAD worker. Set both when CadQuery / Text2CAD
# engines should be available in the prototyping header. Without these,
# /api/cad/generate returns 503 worker_not_configured and only the
# OpenSCAD engine (browser-local) is usable.
# See worker/README.md for deploy steps.
CAD_WORKER_URL=""
CAD_WORKER_SECRET=""
